.SS Common columns (all modes)
.TP
.B Address
The starting virtual address of the mapping, in hex. The mapping
ends at \fIAddress\fR + \fIKbytes\fR (rounded up to the page size).
.TP
.B Kbytes
Size of the mapping in kibibytes.
.TP
.B Mode
A five-character permission string of the form \fBrwxs\-\fR:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
positions 1-3: \fBr\fR / \fBw\fR / \fBx\fR if the mapping permits
read / write / execute, or \fB\-\fR otherwise — see
\fBproc_pid_maps\fR(5).
.IP \(bu 2
position 4: \fBs\fR if the mapping is shared, \fB\-\fR if private.
.IP \(bu 2
position 5: always \fB\-\fR. This slot is preserved for compatibility
with the historical \fBpmap\fR output format and has no current
meaning.
.RE
.TP
.B Mapping
The basename of the file backing the mapping (or the full path with
\fB\-p\fR), or one of the pseudo-mappings listed below.
.SS Extended-mode columns (\-x)
.TP
.B RSS
Resident set size — how much of this mapping is currently in
physical memory, in kibibytes. From \fBRss\fR in
\fI/proc/[pid]/smaps\fR.
.TP
.B Dirty
Modified pages in this mapping that have not been written back, in
kibibytes. Computed as \fBPrivate_Dirty\fR + \fBShared_Dirty\fR from
\fI/proc/[pid]/smaps\fR.
.SS Device-mode columns (\-d)
.TP
.B Offset
Byte offset into the backing file at which this mapping begins.
\fB0\fR for anonymous mappings.
.TP
.B Device
The block device that holds the backing file, formatted as
\fImajor\fR\fB:\fR\fIminor\fR in hexadecimal. \fB000:00000\fR for
anonymous mappings.
.SS Mapping names
.PP
File mappings use the basename, including any \fB(deleted)\fR suffix.
\fB\-p\fR retains the full pathname. Default anonymous labels have two
leading spaces: \fB[ anon ]\fR, or \fB[ stack ]\fR for the mapping
containing the process's starting stack address.
.PP
System V shared-memory mappings show \fB[ shmid=0x\fR\fIID\fR\fB ]\fR,
also preceded by two spaces. The ID is the shared-memory identifier,
not its key.
.PP
\fB\-k\fR preserves kernel bracketed names such as \fB[heap]\fR,
\fB[vdso]\fR, \fB[vvar]\fR, and \fB[vvar_vclock]\fR. Without
\fB\-k\fR these non-file mappings use the anonymous or stack label.
